"DOI":"10.1002/chem.201805626","Year":2019,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-036079","value":"13.6 ± 0.9","numeric":13.6}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-037726","Abbreviation_in_the_article":13,"Cell_line":"A2780","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"3.83 ± 1.44","IC50_Dark_value":3.83,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/cmdc.201600577","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-037726","value":"2.56 ± 1.97","numeric":2.56}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-037727","Abbreviation_in_the_article":13,"Cell_line":"A2780cisR","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"13.15 ± 6.48","IC50_Dark_value":13.15,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/cmdc.201600577","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-037727","value":"27.09 ± 6.35","numeric":27.09}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":13,"value":0.24,"value_relation":"=","std":0.02,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1002/cmdc.201600577","year":2017,"record_id":"MLDB-001865","detection":"ICP-OES","method_description":"LogPow were carried out using the shake flask method.19 PtIV compounds were dissolved in 0.9 % w/v NaCl in ultrapure water (pre-saturated with n-octanol for 96 h and left to stand overnight). The solutions were sonicated and filtered through Celite to remove undissolved PtIV compounds. The initial Pt concentrations were determined by ICP-OES to ascertain the maximum solubility of the complexes. Subsequently, these solutions were added to an equal volume of n-octanol (pre-saturated with 0.9 % w/v NaCl in ultrapure water for 96 h and left to stand overnight) and shaken vigorously for 2 h before centrifuging at 4200 g for 15 min to achieve phase separation. The residual Pt concentrations in the aqueous phase were determined by ICP-OES from which the LogPow was calculated. All experiments were done in triplicate."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"I","value":0.26,"value_relation":"=","std":0.03,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"200 mM NaCl","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1002/chem.201805626","year":2019,"record_id":"MLDB-002152","detection":"FAAS","method_description":"The partition coefficients (P) of the investigated platinum complexes were determined by the “shake flask” method. The complexes were dissolved in octanol-saturated water (OSW) containing 200 mm NaCl and mixed with water-saturated octanol (WSO) in volumetric ratios of 2:1, 1:1, and 1:2. Mixing was done by vortexing for 30 min at room temperature to establish the partition equilibrium. To separate the phases, centrifugation was done at 3000 g for 5 min. The layers were separated carefully by using a fine-tip pipette and then analyzed for metal content by flameless atomic absorption spectroscopy (FAAS). The partition coefficients were calculated as the ratio of the concentration of the compound in the octanol layer to that in the aqueous layer, log P=log ([Pt]WSO/[Pt]OSW)."}]}